            <ArticleTitle>Clinical and radiological deterioration due to Mycobacterium szulgai in an asthmatic patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>89-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 23-year-old asthmatic woman who had clinical and radiological deterioration due to Mycobacterium szulgai infection and good response to anti-mycobacterial treatment without any structural abnormalities in previous lung imaging studies. M. szulgai may be considered a pathogen able to cause deterioration of respiratory health even in patients with previously normal lungs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
